equipment,  it may be impossible to hedge foreign currency exposure with respect
to  residual  values.  This is  because  the amount and timing of receipt of the
residual  interest is  unpredictable  and hedge  contracts  typically  require a
precise  monetary amount and date. Even with leases  requiring rental payment in
U.S.  dollars,  the equipment may be sold at lease expiration for an amount that
cannot be  pre-determined  to a buyer paying in a foreign  currency.  This could
